WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.767
-There are so many things I have
to congratulate you on,

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:04.167
and I on -- I don't know
where to start.

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:09.334
I guess we start with the Oscar
nomination and the win.

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:11.133
-Thank you.
-"The Power of the Dog."

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:15.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah, thank you very much.

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:17.367
You kind of feel that you're
winning when you get

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:19.567
offered a role like that,
for a director like that,

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:21.534
that's a double win and then for
her to win Best Director

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:23.601
for us, we were dancing around
that Oscar.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:26.400
-What was she like to
work with?

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.901
-She's just a trip,
she's so much fun.

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:32.434
She's just very unassuming.

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:34.033
I only knew her for her work,
before I met her.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:35.634
I'd never met her socially.

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:37.434
I had no idea what was going to
walk through the door.

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:39.000
She just came in with a little
rucksack,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.868
"Oh, hi, Ben, how are you?"
Your family is great.

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:44.868
Chatty, everyday, talking about
the weather.

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:46.801
-Did it feel like it
was going to be a big movie or

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:49.634
did if feel like it was kind of
going to be an independent

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:51.133
even though it was
a giant budget?

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:57.400
-I was focused on him, and Phil
Burbank and working with her.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.667
I didn't really think how it
would play out as a movie.

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:03.167
It wasn't really my head space
at all.

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:08.267
-And you were so great and so
creepy almost, I want to say.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:10.200
[ Laughter ]
I don't know how to describe it.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.701
-I get very defensive
about that character,

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:13.300
but I'll still take that
as a compliment.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:16.100
-Yes, yes, yes, yes!
I just know you.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:17.634
And we've done so many bits
on the show.

00:01:17.634 --> 00:01:19.133
You come and you've played
played charades.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:23.901
This was not you.
This was acting 701 right here.

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:26.634
This is like advanced acting
class right here.

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:30.267
I just loved it. Congratulations
on that. That was awesome.

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:32.300
-Thank you very much.
-And I got to see that.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.200
Oh, my gosh, I'm so happy, I
can't wait to congratulate

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.033
you next time I see Benedict.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:38.167
And then
"Spiderman: No Way Home"

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:40.834
goes on to be, like, the biggest
film of all time

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.534
makes, like,
a gazillion dollars.

00:01:42.534 --> 00:01:44.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
It's so much fun.

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:48.767
-Great fun.
-I mean, what was that?

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:50.934
Did you know that was --
-Yeah, I did.

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:54.334
[ Laughter ]
-That one you knew.

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:58.400
-Well, look, it's a testament
to John Watts and the three,

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:02.000
you know, Jacob Z, and Tom,
they've got this beautiful

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.734
John Hughes homage mixed in with
the ultimate universal love,

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:10.334
there is for that, that kid,
that hero, for Spiderman,

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:12.567
and Peter Parker.
And it was such a good script.

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:17.434
Such a good concept. And then
there was that "little secret."

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:18.467
-But it was so much fun to
watch!

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:19.667
-It was so much fun.

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:21.567
And what I think they did so
blindingly well

00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:26.501
was just a mix humor with pathos
to mix surprise with elation

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:29.267
and expectation and confound
expectation.

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:31.267
They just, they managed to pull
off a huge feat.

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:33.601
Which, apart from anything else
because of throwing in Toby

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:37.000
and Andrew,
it meant you were celebrating

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.501
like 20 years worth of film
making on top of all that.

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:41.567
It was a real punch.
-It was a moment.

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:45.234
I thought it was great. And then
we'll talk about Dr. Strange --

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:48.133
but also you're hosting
"Saturday Night Live" again

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:50.901
which I'm so happy to hear.
-So excited.

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:52.901
-The building is buzzing that
you're in the building.

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:54.234
And Arcade Fire.

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:57.334
-One of my all-time favorite,
favorite bands.

00:02:57.334 --> 00:03:00.968
I heard him last time,
he was incredible.

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:02.968
These guys I've been following
since they first began.

00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:06.100
I feel like --
-Anything different

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.601
you're going to do the second
time around?

00:03:07.601 --> 00:03:10.400
-Yep, breathe and enjoy it more.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:13.033
It goes so quickly. You kind of
watch the tape the next day.

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:15.601
Going, "Was it any good?"
You have no idea.

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:17.968
You're at the call at 11:30
at night.

00:03:17.968 --> 00:03:21.133
Even for stage work, that's when
you're coming off the stage

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.567
for who you meet up with

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:24.734
and have a drink or something to
eat before going home.

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:28.601
That's just when you're going to
work on "Saturday Night Live."

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:30.100
It's so weird.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.601
-It's one of the rare live
television,

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:33.200
I don't know if they
do live any more.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.667
-Nothing like it, that's why I
wanted to do it again.

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:38.901
-Once you do it, the
book, the chapter is over.

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:41.133
The book is closed and you go--
but you were fantastic.

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:42.701
So, break a leg.
I know they're all writing,

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:43.868
they all psyched
that you're here.

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:45.601
Congratulations on that.
-Very excited, too.

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:49.968
-Let's talk about
"Dr. Strange."

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:52.534
With Marvel movies on our show,
normally we're not allowed to

00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:57.133
talk about anything.
Has it changed, has it changed.

00:03:57.133 --> 00:03:58.634
Are we allowed to talk about
anything?

00:03:58.634 --> 00:03:59.968
-No, I'm basically here to
talk about a movie

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:01.701
I can't talk about.
-Yeah, perfect.

00:04:01.701 --> 00:04:04.267
-So how do we talk about a movie
that we can't talk about?

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:06.334
-Well.
-It's coming out.

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.834
-I mean maybe.
-Can we say that? on Friday.

00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:11.467
-You, yeah that's true. That is
actually what's happening.

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:13.901
-It will be out
and revealed to the world.

00:04:13.901 --> 00:04:16.367
-And then, you know --
-It will be projected.

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:18.267
-There's some people in it.
Some people in the film.

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:20.767
-Humans?
-Mainly, yeah.

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:22.334
-Yeah? Mainly humans
are in the film.

00:04:22.334 --> 00:04:25.334
And, uh, Imax?
-Yes, that is apparently

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:27.200
somewhere it will be exhibited.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:31.133
-Yes. Sounds great.
-2-D and 3-D.

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:33.467
-Oh, and 3-D?
-It'll have sound. And music.

00:04:33.467 --> 00:04:35.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:38.434
-There's rumors that there might
be a cameo or two in there.

00:04:38.434 --> 00:04:43.100
-Okay, well, look, I guess I am
on the Fallon show, so maybe,

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.934
maybe, Jimmy, I can just, just
one clue as to somebody

00:04:45.934 --> 00:04:49.067
who may be in the film because
it's coming out quite soon.

00:04:49.067 --> 00:04:51.367
I'm not going to say their name.
-Okay.

00:04:51.367 --> 00:04:54.667
-But, I'll see if you can guess
it from a theme tune.

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:57.801
Of something else that they've
done that's quite well-known.

00:04:57.801 --> 00:05:00.901
Ready?
-Hmm. Okay.

00:05:00.901 --> 00:05:10.434
-[ Hums theme song ]
-Okay, really?!

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:11.934
-No.
-Okay, wow.

00:05:11.934 --> 00:05:16.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:18.834
-That was pretty good,
by the way.

00:05:18.834 --> 00:05:20.634
-Aren't you disappointed people
that bought their ticket

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:22.968
wanting to see two Tom Cruises
films in one month.

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:26.834
[ Laughter ]
-Tom Cruise's not right?

00:05:26.834 --> 00:05:31.868
-Yeah, yeah, it's very good.
-In these films you do

00:05:31.868 --> 00:05:33.167
your fight scenes --
-Yes.

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:36.934
-With very like, you
have the sorcerer-type moves.

00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:38.267
-Gestures.
-Gestures.

00:05:38.267 --> 00:05:41.901
-I'm sure you've been trained to
do these.

00:05:41.901 --> 00:05:43.167
-Endlessly.
-Yeah?

00:05:43.167 --> 00:05:46.467
-It's hard work. Yeah.
-That wasn't my question.

00:05:46.467 --> 00:05:49.601
-Oh, what was your question?
Sorry? "Is it hard work?"

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:52.033
-Is it hard work?
-It is.

00:05:52.033 --> 00:05:53.868
-No, but I mean I always thought
maybe you could teach me

00:05:53.868 --> 00:05:56.934
a move or two maybe tonight if
you could show me how --

00:05:56.934 --> 00:05:58.868
-I think the best way to do
this, probably,

00:05:58.868 --> 00:06:01.400
because this is, like
the sixth time I've played him.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.367
So I, you know, you get some
perks after awhile.

00:06:03.367 --> 00:06:06.667
And one of them is that I don't
do the hand moves any more.

00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:09.567
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:06:09.567 --> 00:06:13.534
-In this film Sam Raimi does
them, so what you need to do

00:06:13.534 --> 00:06:16.801
is you need to be me, right?
I need you to stand up.

00:06:16.801 --> 00:06:20.000
And just sort of put your hands
behind your back a little bit

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.601
so that people think these brown
arms are yours.

00:06:23.601 --> 00:06:26.567
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.567 --> 00:06:29.434
-Well, Jimmy, it's just an
excuse for us to hug really.

00:06:29.434 --> 00:06:32.667
-I don't want this to
end, yeah. I really don't.

00:06:32.667 --> 00:06:36.667
Oh, my goodness. Well, hey,
let's go into this portal

00:06:36.667 --> 00:06:42.767
over there and then we can go --
you know, I'm a little thirsty.

00:06:51.634 --> 00:06:55.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.367
-Thank you very much.
Just a little thirsty.

00:06:57.367 --> 00:07:02.434
Now, I want to tell you all more
about Dr. Strange,

00:07:02.434 --> 00:07:05.934
but I really can't.
I'd rather just --

00:07:05.934 --> 00:07:08.734
I can't tell but
I can show you a clip.

00:07:08.734 --> 00:07:11.968
So, ladies and gentlemen,
here is Benedict Cumberbatch

00:07:11.968 --> 00:07:15.167
in "Dr. Strange in the
Multiverse of Madness!"

00:07:15.167 --> 00:07:17.601
Take a look!

00:07:17.601 --> 00:07:21.634
♪♪

00:07:21.634 --> 00:07:23.734
[ Screaming ]

00:07:23.734 --> 00:07:27.601
♪♪

00:07:27.601 --> 00:07:29.734
-Whoa!

00:07:29.734 --> 00:07:31.901
♪♪

00:07:31.901 --> 00:07:34.234
-[ Monster roars ]

00:07:34.234 --> 00:07:36.767
-[ Yells ]
Oh, no!

00:07:36.767 --> 00:07:38.334
-[ Grunts ]

00:07:38.334 --> 00:07:46.567
♪♪

00:07:46.567 --> 00:07:50.334
[ Grunting ]

00:07:50.334 --> 00:07:54.267
-Look out!

00:07:54.267 --> 00:07:58.567
[ Whirs ]
-[ Grunts ]

00:08:01.267 --> 00:08:04.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I can't wait! This weekend!

00:08:04.834 --> 00:08:06.567
Benedict Cumberbatch, everybody!

00:08:06.567 --> 00:08:09.868
"Dr. Strange in the Multiverse
of Madness!"

00:08:09.868 --> 00:08:12.133
Opens in theaters and IMAX
this Friday.

00:08:12.133 --> 00:08:14.067
And he hosts
"Saturday Night Live"

00:08:14.067 --> 00:08:16.801
with musical guest Arcane Fire,
this weekend!

